## One thing the operator must weigh before submitting
The reel reports `durationTicks 18001` against this contract's `18000`-tick envelope, so the door will very likely refuse it `reel_duration_exceeded`. `e7-relay-rush` declares no `twist.secureWave`, so `PlaybookFormat.runTapeEnvelopeForContract` skips its `+2` inclusive-endpoint slack and grants a flat `MAX_PLAYBOOK_TICKS`; the secure lands at wave 20 = tick 18000 and the `SECURE_CHOICE` is recorded there. **No rider policy avoids this** — same defect that refused generations 24 and 25, now confirmed on a third epoch. It's recorded in `gauntlet-outcome.json.doorRisk` with the line of code.

